index 00000000..f95c1987
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/fsdp-init.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# FSDPTurbo backend: initialization milestone
+
+This experimental entry initializes Slime training actors using FSDPTurbo's
+Python environment. It does not load a model, train GRPO, generate responses,
+publish weights, or save checkpoints yet. Those operations fail explicitly.
+
+Run the driver with the original serving Python. Pass an absolute training
+Python path using `--fsdp-python-executable`; only training Ray actors receive
+that interpreter. The same checkout and training environment must be visible
+to the actors. This milestone supports one node only.
+
+Example inside an already configured Ray/NPU environment:
+
+```bash
+python train.py \
+  --train-backend fsdp --fsdp-provider fsdpturbo --fsdp-init-only \
+  --fsdp-python-executable /workspace/slime-fsdp2/envs/fsdp2/bin/python \
+  --fsdp-init-report /tmp/fsdp-init-result.json \
+  --actor-num-nodes 1 --actor-num-gpus-per-node 2 --num-gpus-per-node 4 \
+  --rollout-batch-size 2 --distributed-backend hccl
+```
+
+The check uses Slime's placement groups and training actor factory. Two training
+devices run FP32/BF16 all-reduce, all-gather and reduce-scatter with exact expected
+results. A CPU Ray worker imports SGLang ServerArgs with the driver's interpreter;
+this is an environment check, not a running SGLang engine or generation test.
+Training groups are shut down, actors killed, and placements released afterward.
+
+The FSDP parser and actor module import do not require Megatron, MegatronAdaptor,
+TransformerEngine or SGLang. The provider itself has a different boundary:
+FSDPTurbo `fsdp_turbo/ops/__init__.py` attempts CUDA registration even on NPU,
+and its CUDA permute/RMSNorm modules optionally import TransformerEngine.
+The runtime report records those optional imports separately. It does not claim
+that the complete FSDPTurbo process is free of TransformerEngine imports.
+Megatron, MegatronAdaptor and SGLang must remain absent from training actors.
+
+Validated environment: original Python uses Transformers 5.12.1; training venv
+uses Transformers 5.16.0. Torch/TorchNPU remain the image-provided 2.10 versions.
+TorchAO native extensions are unavailable in this environment; quantized training
+is outside this milestone. Native extension compilation may slow first startup.
+
+Rejected configurations include offload, colocation, critic/PPO, reference/KL,
+OPD, fault tolerance, checkpoint load/save, routing replay and non-object-store
+rollout transport. The GRPO option here selects the intended future algorithm;
+no GRPO loss is computed during initialization.
+
+The existing Megatron entry remains the default. Its checkpoint fallback is
+backend-specific; FSDP initialization starts with an empty restore plan. Tests
+cover strict CLI validation and lazy imports in `tests/test_fsdp_entry.py`.
